  "adaptation": {
    "semantic": "\"smash\": the breaking sense (*smash a glass*) and the hitting sense (*smash into a tree*) are often two different verbs in other languages. In *smash a record* nothing is destroyed: the record is beaten by a lot.",
    "grammar": "\"smash\" can have the broken thing as its subject with no object (*the glass smashed*); many languages need a reflexive or passive form here.",
